      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CURTIS KEEPING (8) jumped well to win over the 400m at Dubbo two runs back then raced on speed again when finishing second at Dubbo last start. Solid beginner and with a good start should have clear running out wide. Good form should continue. BALL OF SMOKE (6) missed the frame latest when fifth at Wagga (31.18) but scored four back at this track (26.12). Returns to favourable track. Speedy beginner who can find the front despite the tricky draw. Cannot be underestimated. FINE SHINE (1) looks close to another win after finishing third from Box 4 last time (26.15) at this track. Boasts three wins from six starts out of this box. Bold showing expected. FLASH BANDIT (2) should be in the finish fresh from a three months break.",
